WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.838 --> 00:00:03.720
- All right y'all, I'm back
with producer extraordinaire

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.890
Norman Lear.
- Yes!

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.420
- And you know my next guest
as the hilarious scene stealer

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.150
from "The Mindy Project".

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.530
Her new Netflix special, "Sweet and Salty"

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:16.363
is out right now.

00:00:16.363 --> 00:00:17.400
Take a look.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.010
- My entire family
loved eating at Hooters.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.810
Even my mom liked eating at Hooters

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.540
because you could buy a wheel barrow

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.320
of wings for four dollars.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.907
She's like, "Everybody's rich at Hooters".

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.120
However she wasn't always willing to admit

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.669
that she liked Hooters.

00:00:34.669 --> 00:00:38.323
I have been to Hooters my entire life.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:42.490
Not with me, I have never

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.343
been to Hooters.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:51.814
I'm like, "You recruited my
babysitter at a Hooters".

00:00:51.814 --> 00:00:55.262
(laughs)
(audience cheering)

00:00:55.262 --> 00:00:58.552
- Please welcome Fortune Feimster.

00:00:58.552 --> 00:01:00.769
(happy music)

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:03.769
(audience clapping)

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:16.069
- That's for you.

00:01:16.069 --> 00:01:17.569
- All right.
- Yes!

00:01:19.508 --> 00:01:22.291
Have a seat.
- Okay, thank you.

00:01:22.291 --> 00:01:23.880
- Hi!
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.530
- Ah, you're so funny!
- Thank you!

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.380
- Oh my god, I love you.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.483
Meet Norman Lear, yes.

00:01:27.483 --> 00:01:28.316
- How are you?

00:01:28.316 --> 00:01:29.497
- Oh I'm so-
- Ow!

00:01:29.497 --> 00:01:31.050
(laughs)

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.910
- I'm so strong.
- He was cracking up.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:33.860
We're both cracking up
- Oh good!

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.700
- watching you and your
Hooters spiel, I love it.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.480
- I'm between two legends, right now.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.024
- No, not the same, not the same at all.

00:01:41.024 --> 00:01:43.580
- Oh my gosh, what a treat.
- I'll take it,

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.580
but totally a lie.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.100
Your accent always reminds me of home.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.960
I always love when I run into you.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:49.793
It just feels-

00:01:49.793 --> 00:01:50.880
So where did you grow up?

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.080
- I grew up in North Carolina.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.007
My mom made me be a debutant,
that's how southern I am.

00:01:55.007 --> 00:01:57.100
- You're a southern bell.
- I am.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.280
- You're a southern bell,
wait what did that entail.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.113
What did you have to do?

00:02:00.113 --> 00:02:01.590
Oh my gosh!

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.787
- [Fortune] I was like, "what happened!?".

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.560
- You are so fancy right now!

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.840
- Yeah, I had to wear
a white wedding gown.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.910
- Oh my god, you were
like from the bricks,

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:11.890
I was from the sticks, girl.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.820
We didn't have anything like that.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.710
- But we had no money.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:17.540
That was the thing, my mom had been one

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.960
and then we lost all our money.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.490
It happens.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.323
- It happens!

00:02:22.323 --> 00:02:23.879
- You know, gambling.

00:02:23.879 --> 00:02:26.270
(laughing)

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:28.590
And then she still wanted me to carry on

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.640
this tradition of being a,

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.230
pretending to be rich and
then go to etiquette classes.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.407
- That's amazing.
- Etiquette classes?

00:02:36.407 --> 00:02:38.337
- Yeah, I had to learn how to be a lady.

00:02:38.337 --> 00:02:41.360
(laughter)

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.423
I didn't know, I didn't
know, I had to like-

00:02:43.423 --> 00:02:47.360
- I don't!
- Dab my face with a napkin.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.053
You know, you just can't wipe
your face like a monster!

00:02:50.053 --> 00:02:52.020
(laughing)

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.160
- Obviously I didn't
attend etiquette classes.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.870
- All right, well I still to this day,

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.790
people are like, "You
should never eat in public".

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:01.697
'Cause it's not great.
(laughing)

